{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1224221-can-you-explain-who-could-the-prophets-of-fajad-be","id":1224221,"title":"Can you explain who could the Prophets of Fajad be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-02T13:33:11-07:00","id":1224221,"title":"Can you explain who could the Prophets of Fajad be?","content":"I am currently writing up Fajad as the next big setting in my upcoming campaign. While all of my mortal and exalted npcs are ready I still can't crack the prophets. Are they gods that dencounced godhood to make themselves more appealing? Honored ancestors and if so then why the Wyld hunt or the Immaculate didn't send an exorcist or two? If they are gods wouldn't it make beings in Yu Shan angry that they steal faith from rightful divinities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3658-mr-miracle","name":"Mr Miracle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T13:51:49-07:00","id":1224226,"title":"","content":"I think they're a combination of ghosts and gods? And I think their faith is generally supposed to be taken as sincere.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Immaculate Order and Yu-Shan aren't all powerful, they can't take apart every heresy that comes along, particularly when it would be strong and attached to a lucrative spot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T15:03:42-07:00","id":1224235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Miracle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1224221-can-you-explain-who-could-the-prophets-of-fajad-be#post1224221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am currently writing up Fajad as the next big setting in my upcoming campaign. While all of my mortal and exalted npcs are ready I still can't crack the prophets. Are they gods that dencounced godhood to make themselves more appealing? Honored ancestors and if so then why the Wyld hunt or the Immaculate didn't send an exorcist or two? If they are gods wouldn't it make beings in Yu Shan angry that they steal faith from rightful divinities?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While all prophets alive are gods and disciples of the writings of a long dead mystic, it is possible for ghosts and mortals to play a similair role. I mean, the book says &quot;spirits&quot; so they could be lementals or demons, I suppose.<br /> <br /> As for Exorcists, because the Abhari are zealous enough that a Wyld Hunt would cause a revolt the Empress didn't want to deal with.<br /> As for Yu Shuan, the Heavens are rather bad at stopping corruption, even if this isn't a sincere creed. How YuShuan deals with Hetero-orthodox opinions on the cosmos among divinities will be intreasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}